{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And Jacob told, etc.</b> Meaning: he told her of two dimensions of kinship that Rachel had — one, kinship of body, which is what the verse says <b>for he is her father's brother</b>; and the second, kinship of soul, which is what the verse says <b>and that he is Rebecca's son</b> — and Rebecca was known for her righteous deeds, and the righteous rejoice in those who are like them." "<b>Further,</b> it alludes in the manner of what they said, of blessed memory (Megillah 13b), that her father said to him [Laban said to Jacob] that he [Laban] was a deceiver, and he [Jacob] replied that he [too] was his brother in deception. And accordingly, Jacob felt concerned lest it be said of him that it is a disgrace for a righteous person to conduct himself with a wicked person according to his wickedness; therefore he said <b>and that he is Rebecca's son</b> — meaning that he would outwit him in a way of justice and truth, to make him disgorge [his deceit] from his mouth and to defeat him in his own judgments. And this is the sod of (Ecclesiastes 7:12–13) ״הַחָכְמָה תְּחַיֶּה בְעָלֶיהָ״ — that he would not deceive him in a way of wickedness and repulsiveness that would bring him shame in acting thus."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:34.589407872Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}